import csv, html, json, statistics, sys
sys.path.insert(0,"/tmp/ossomex-article-deps")
from pathlib import Path
from run import ROOT, OUT, save
from jsonl_io import rows

def load(p,default=None):return json.loads(Path(p).read_text()) if Path(p).exists() else default

def pct(v):return '—' if v is None else f'{100*v:.1f}'
def table(headers,records):return '\n'.join(['| '+' | '.join(headers)+' |','|'+'|'.join('---' for _ in headers)+'|']+['| '+' | '.join(map(str,row))+' |' for row in records])
LABEL={'ossomex012':'OSSoMeX 012','wapiti':'Softcite Wapiti','scibert':'Softcite SciBERT'}
def main():
 summaries=load(OUT/'summary.json',[])+load(OUT/'corrected/summary.json',[])
 primary=[r for r in summaries if r['dataset']!='softcite-gold-documents' and r.get('f1') is not None and r['policy']==('native' if r['arm']=='ossomex012' else 'explicit')]
 coverage=load(OUT/'coverage-diagnostics.json',[]);timing=load(OUT/'timing-summary.json',[]);boot=load(OUT/'paired-bootstrap.json',[])
 sections=['# OSSoMeX 012 vs Softcite Wapiti and SciBERT',
 'Fresh local benchmark run · 2 October 2026' + (' · IN PROGRESS' if 'COMPLETE ALL' not in (OUT/'queue.log').read_text() else ''),
 '## Findings',
 'No model wins every benchmark. 012 leads the point estimates on fresh30, exposed50, and regression7; Wapiti has a narrow lead on reserve27. Both Softcite models substantially outperform 012 on the recovered paragraph gold. The small OpenAlex samples and provisional labels do not establish a general winner; fresh30 is consistent with either model leading on another sample.',
 'OSSoMeX also has higher selected-set recall on corrected SoMeSci (104/145 names, versus 53 Wapiti and 74 SciBERT) and corrected SoFAIR (91/120, versus 8 and 46 under the explicitly labelled whitespace sensitivity). These subsets lack audited negative coverage, so this is recall evidence, not an established precision/F1 advantage. Catalogue matches on the 20-paper set are 367/666 for OSSoMeX, 35 for Wapiti and 267 for SciBERT.',
 'OSSoMeX has a useful version-linking advantage on the seven regression excerpts, while sentiment and aliases still need stronger supervision. The detector needs better recall and fewer false positives, and the dense package-list timing outlier exposes excessive pairwise work. The highest-priority next experiment is to remove contradictory negative training copies and evaluate a source-balanced training mixture.',
 'Only 012 was freshly evaluated among the OSSoMeX checkpoints. These results do not establish it as the best internal checkpoint across domains.',
 '## What was compared',
 'All three models were rerun on the same frozen source windows. OSSoMeX ran all five stages on Apple MPS; Softcite ran in its two existing amd64 CPU containers. No model weights, thresholds, or production source files were changed. Each input is split into at most 480 SciBERT content tokens with 64-token overlap. Warmup and explicit accelerator synchronization follow the general measurement guidance in [PyTorch’s benchmarking recipe](https://docs.pytorch.org/tutorials/recipes/recipes/benchmark). These results describe this matched-window harness, including its handling of overlap; they are not whole-document pipeline measurements.',
 'The inventory covers 13 existing input populations plus repaired SoMeSci10 and SoFAIR6 imports, followed by three warm timing repeats on fresh30. Repeated versions of the same historical population are not treated as independent benchmarks. The original legacy imports are retained only for operational diagnostics because their offsets are broken.',
 '## Exact software-name results',
 'Percentages below use exact span matching and the reference coverage masks. Predictions in explicitly unjudged regions are excluded, not labelled false positives. For Softcite the main comparison uniformly includes language fields and excludes software-name entries marked implicit. Native-field results follow separately. OpenAlex and regression labels are provisional and exposed during development. The Softcite paragraphs and documents represent overlapping gold, so do not pool their counts or average their scores as independent evidence.',
 table(['Dataset','Model','TP','FP','FN','Precision %','Recall %','F1 %'],[[r['dataset'],LABEL[r['arm']],r['tp'],r['fp'],r['fn'],pct(r['precision']),pct(r['recall']),pct(r['f1'])] for r in primary]),
 '![Exact name F1](name-f1.png)',
 '## Controlled whitespace replay',
 'Both Softcite engines returned incorrect positions for SPSS after just one leading space in a synthetic probe. The original document-gold pass has many unaligned native names and is not ranked by occurrence F1. The replay removes leading whitespace from each affected window for all three models, advances its source offset by exactly that amount, and maps all predictions back to the unchanged original document. Unchanged windows reuse their identical responses from this fresh run. This adds no independent test data. The full protocol and raw responses remain available in `whitespace-control/` and `whitespace-offset-probe.json`.',
 table(['Dataset','Model','TP','FP','FN','Precision %','Recall %','F1 %','Name alignment issues'],[[r['dataset'],LABEL[r['arm']],r.get('tp','—'),r.get('fp','—'),r.get('fn','—'),pct(r.get('precision')),pct(r.get('recall')),pct(r.get('f1')),r['name_alignment_issues']] for r in load(OUT/'whitespace-control/summary.json',[]) if r['policy']==('native' if r['arm']=='ossomex012' else 'explicit')]),
 'In fresh30, six OSSoMeX predictions and three Wapiti predictions fall in an explicitly unjudged passage containing SOVAT and SPSS-GIS. They are uniformly excluded by the frozen software-coverage mask; SciBERT returned none there. Those candidates need adjudication and must not be treated as either established true positives or established false positives.',
 '### Posthoc whitespace-normalization sensitivity',
 'This additional analysis uses the same replay responses, with no further inference. It trims only boundary whitespace inside the supplied native range and accepts internal whitespace differences only when the complete range and returned name match after whitespace normalization. Original source characters are retained. It does not search for strings, move across non-whitespace characters, or consult gold labels. OSSoMeX outputs had no boundary whitespace. This is a posthoc integration sensitivity, not a replacement for the strict primary protocol or an independent test set. See `whitespace-canonical/normalization-audit.json` and `score_whitespace_canonical.py`.',
 table(['Dataset','Model','TP','FN','Precision %','Recall %','F1 %','Unresolved names'],[[r['dataset'],LABEL[r['arm']],r.get('tp','—'),r.get('fn','—'),pct(r.get('precision')),pct(r.get('recall')),pct(r.get('f1')),r['name_alignment_issues']] for r in load(OUT/'whitespace-canonical/summary.json',[]) if r.get('gold_names') is not None and r['policy']==('native' if r['arm']=='ossomex012' else 'explicit')]),
 '## Native Softcite sensitivity',
 table(['Dataset','Model','Native F1 %','Explicit-name F1 %'],[[r['dataset'],LABEL[r['arm']],pct(next((v.get('f1') for v in summaries if v['dataset']==r['dataset'] and v['arm']==r['arm'] and v['policy']=='native'),None)),pct(r['f1'])] for r in primary if r['arm']!='ossomex012']),
 '## Positive-only and catalogue diagnostics',
 'These are recall or coverage measurements with different denominators, not precision/F1 benchmarks. The repaired corpus marks negative coverage as unaudited. Catalogue coverage uses complete native name strings even when position alignment fails, because catalogue links have no offsets. Catalogue links may refer to names absent from the recovered text or to different spellings. The diverse-excerpt list is curated and incomplete. The dev190 query seeds are search targets, not independent annotations.',
 table(['Dataset','Model','Matched / reference','Recall or coverage %'],[[r['dataset'],LABEL[r['arm']],f"{r['tp']} / {r['gold_names']}",pct(r['recall'])] for r in summaries if r['dataset'].endswith('corrected') and r['policy']==('native' if r['arm']=='ossomex012' else 'explicit')]+[[r['dataset'],LABEL[r['arm']],f"{r['hits']} / {r['total']}",pct(r['hits']/r['total'])] for r in coverage if r.get('policy') in [None,'explicit'] or r['arm']=='ossomex012']),
 '### Diverse excerpts by topic',
 table(['Topic','OSSoMeX matches','Wapiti matches','SciBERT matches','Candidate count'],[[p['topic'],p['hits'],next((q['hits'] for r in coverage if r['dataset']=='diverse10-excerpts' and r['arm']=='wapiti' for q in r['per_document'] if q['topic']==p['topic']),'—'),next((q['hits'] for r in coverage if r['dataset']=='diverse10-excerpts' and r['arm']=='scibert' for q in r['per_document'] if q['topic']==p['topic']),'—'),p['total']] for r in coverage if r['dataset']=='diverse10-excerpts' and r['arm']=='ossomex012' for p in r['per_document']]),
 '## Position-free name sensitivity',
 'These diagnostic scores compare distinct, case-sensitive name strings per document, ignoring offsets and repeated occurrences. They help distinguish recognition from native offset failures but cannot substitute for occurrence F1 or version-link evaluation. Only the document-gold set has exhaustive name coverage in this table; repaired SoMeSci/SoFAIR values are recall only.',
 table(['Dataset','Model','Distinct-name precision %','Distinct-name recall %','Distinct-name F1 %'],[[r['dataset'],LABEL[r['arm']],pct(r['precision']),pct(r['recall']),pct(r['f1'])] for r in load(OUT/'surface-diagnostics.json',[]) if r['dataset'] in ['softcite-gold-documents','somesci10-corrected','sofair6-corrected'] and r['policy']==('native' if r['arm']=='ossomex012' else 'explicit')]),
 '## Versions and full attributes',
 'Version spans and name–version links are different tasks. These tables use exact positions and native Softcite associations. Softcite supports name-linked versions and usage/creation/sharing context; sentiment and aliases are unsupported. A zero-positive slice cannot establish successful version extraction.',
 table(['Dataset','Model','Version span TP/FP/FN','Span F1 %','Linked version TP/FP/FN','Link F1 %'],[[r['dataset'],LABEL[r['arm']],'/'.join(str(r['version_span_score'][k]) for k in ['tp','fp','fn']),pct(r['version_span_score']['f1']),'/'.join(str(r['version_link_score'][k]) for k in ['tp','fp','fn']),pct(r['version_link_score']['f1'])] for r in primary if 'version_span_score' in r])]
 attrs=[]
 for r in primary:
  if r['dataset'] not in ['fresh30','exposed50','reserve27']:continue
  m=load(OUT/r['dataset']/f"metrics-{r['arm']}-{r['policy']}.json")
  attrs.append([r['dataset'],LABEL[r['arm']],pct(m['intents']['exact_set_accuracy']),pct(m['sentiment']['observed_macro_f1']),pct(m['sentiment']['false_opinion_rate']),pct(m['complete_occurrence']['f1'])])
 sections += [table(['Dataset','Model','Intent exact-set accuracy %','Sentiment observed macro-F1 %','False-opinion rate %','Complete-record F1 %'],attrs),
 'Intent exact-set accuracy includes missed eligible gold mentions; matched-only accuracy is available in the detailed metrics. Observed sentiment macro-F1 excludes classes with no support and must not be called full four-class macro-F1. The exact eligibility masks and per-class support are saved with each metric. Complete-record F1 covers names, versions, intent, and sentiment on eligible references; it does not include aliases. Alias accuracy is not established by these name benchmarks.',
 '## Timing',
 'Each arm was warmed and then run three times over the same 30 snippets in matched randomized order, without concurrent benchmark inference. Loading and warmup are excluded. GPU synchronization is included for OSSoMeX. MPS versus emulated/container CPU is a deployment comparison, not a hardware-controlled architectural speed claim.',
 table(['Model','Measured snippets','No-name responses','Median ms','P95 ms','Snippets/s'],[[LABEL[r['arm']],r['observations'],r.get('responses_without_explicit_names','—'),f"{r['median_ms']:.1f}",f"{r['p95_ms']:.1f}",f"{r['windows_per_second']:.2f}"] for r in timing]),
 'Wapiti has the lowest median but many responses contain no explicit names, so downstream extraction work varies by model. OSSoMeX has the highest measured throughput and lowest P95 on these snippets. Interpret all three timing statistics alongside extraction quality; a fast empty response is not a successful recovery of a labelled mention.',
 'A dense package-list window took roughly 90 seconds in the first OSSoMeX pass: 31 names ×31 versions produced 961 linker candidates, plus 465 alias pairs. The full pipeline currently runs those classifier examples individually. Typical short-snippet speed therefore conceals a substantial tail-latency problem. See `slow-window-example.json` for the exact text, spans, timing, and stage counts.',
 '![Warm latency](warm-latency.png)',
 '### Quality-run timings by dataset',
 'These are the recorded sequential inference times from the quality passes, including failed requests but excluding loading and serialization. Windows vary in length and mention density. Early diagnostic probes overlapped part of the Wapiti quality pass; use the isolated warm repeats above for the primary speed comparison. Do not pool overlapping dataset representations.',
 table(['Dataset','Model','Windows','Inference seconds','Median window ms','P95 window ms'],[[r['dataset'],LABEL[r['arm']],r['windows'],f"{r['seconds']:.1f}",f"{1000*r['median_window_seconds']:.1f}",f"{1000*r['p95_window_seconds']:.1f}"] for r in summaries if r['policy']==('native' if r['arm']=='ossomex012' else 'explicit')]),
 '### Native CPU control',
 table(['Model/device','Observations','Median ms','P95 ms','Snippets/s'],[['OSSoMeX012 · native ARM CPU, four threads',c['observations'],f"{c['median_ms']:.1f}",f"{c['p95_ms']:.1f}",f"{c['windows_per_second']:.2f}"] for c in [load(OUT/'timing/cpu-control-summary.json')] if c]),
 'The CPU control removes the MPS accelerator difference but still compares native ARM PyTorch with amd64 Softcite in Docker; it does not equalize architecture, libraries, or container resources.',
 'The 90 native-CPU observations had the same name, version, intent, sentiment and completion decisions as their matched MPS observations. This check excludes floating-point scores and aliases; see `timing/device-decision-comparison.json`.',
 '## Confidence in model differences',
 'The table reports paired bootstrap intervals for OSSoMeX minus each baseline, resampling input documents 5,000 times with seed 1234. Paragraph-gold intervals resample the 233 source articles, keeping all paragraphs from each sampled article together. Bootstrap counts use the same reference coverage masks as the main scores. These intervals quantify sample variation only; they do not fix provisional labels, test exposure, domain selection, or multiple comparisons.',
 table(['Dataset','Comparison','F1 difference, points','95% interval, points'],[[r['dataset'],r['comparison'],f"{100*r['delta_f1']:+.1f}",f"[{100*r['bootstrap_95_percent_interval'][0]:+.1f}, {100*r['bootstrap_95_percent_interval'][1]:+.1f}]"] for r in boot]),
 '[Side-by-side source cases](examples.html) · [Browse error contexts](errors.html) · [Concrete next-experiment plan](next-experiments.md)\n\nAlias diagnostic: the three selected provisional positive pairs (one in fresh30 and two in exposed50) were all missed by 012. No exhaustive alias precision estimate is available; Softcite does not expose a comparable alias head.',
 '## Detector training exposure',
 'The reconstructed 012 detector pool contains 900 records from 814 articles, with 2,869 software-name annotations: 1,117 exact strings or 1,045 after case folding and whitespace collapse. These are surface-name counts, not unique software projects. Ablation copies are excluded; the other heads have separate training provenance.',
 'The draw log records 896 original record IDs and 121 ablated-copy IDs. Of 7,840 sampled draws, 926 used ablated copies. Source-record vocabulary counts do not prove every annotated span appeared in a sampled window. Checkpoint selection was the fixed final epoch with no development-set selection (`fixed_final_epoch_no_dev`).',
 table(['Dataset','Name seen in detector training','Reference mentions','Exact hits','Recall %'],[[r['dataset'],'yes' if r['name_seen_in_detector_training'] else 'no',r['gold_mentions'],r['exact_hits'],pct(r['recall'])] for r in load(OUT/'training-vocabulary-diagnostic.json',{}).get('recall_by_name_exposure',[])]),
 'This is descriptive recall on the existing exposed evaluations, not a controlled unseen-name test. The packaged baseline training membership is unavailable. Familiar-name misses show that adding vocabulary alone will not resolve all errors; contextual supervision and boundaries also need attention.',
 '## Boundary-error candidates',
 'These counts identify covered false-positive spans that overlap missed reference names. They are review candidates, not relaxed true positives; overlap can still select the wrong entity. The exact-span ranking above is unchanged.',
 table(['Dataset','Model','All FP','FP overlapping a missed name','All FN','FN overlapping an inexact prediction'],[[r['dataset'],LABEL[r['arm']],r['false_positives'],r['fp_overlapping_a_missed_reference'],r['false_negatives'],r['fn_overlapping_an_inexact_prediction']] for r in load(OUT/'boundary-diagnostics.json',[])]),
 '## What to improve next',
 '1. **Remove contradictory detector supervision, then measure the effect.** The adaptation trainer duplicates some unchanged positive texts with no annotations and complete coverage (`train_detector.py`, lines 137–139). The recorded ablation fraction is 15%. Retrain a controlled candidate with this disabled; preserve real negative passages and keep the test split fixed. This is a plausible cause of missed names, not a measured causal explanation yet.',
 '2. **Balance domains and checkpoint selection.** Keep a mixed training pool covering scientific packages, engineering, geospatial, computational humanities, statistical tools, programming languages, model names, and ordinary-word negatives. Select checkpoints using a prespecified multi-domain development criterion. Version012 is the requested candidate; this experiment does not establish that it is the best OSSoMeX checkpoint across domains. Compare006/008/012 under the same repaired protocol before selecting a replacement.',
 'The 900-record detector training pool contains only two annotated literal `Python` occurrences, six `Java`, and no literal `NumPy`; `MATLAB` has 27. These case-sensitive counts come from `training-label-audit.json`, before ablation copies. The training script initializes from base SciBERT rather than continuing the earlier OSSoMeX detector, so broad-domain competence must be represented in this training pool. Some unlabelled source occurrences are legitimate creator/URL negatives, while others merit annotation review; do not label every string match as software.',
 '3. **Improve boundaries and name–version associations.** Add adjudicated examples for adjacent names/versions, dotted and hyphenated versions, package lists, abbreviated names, and multilingual punctuation. The dense-window example includes truncations such as `0.2-` and `1.28.`. Train with exact-span boundary targets and hard competing-version negatives. Report both span F1 and link F1. Audit subword/label alignment explicitly; [Hugging Face’s token-classification guide](https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/tasks/token_classification) describes that alignment step.',
 '4. **Make intent and sentiment datasets independent and larger.** Add human-reviewed created/shared and positive/negative/mixed examples from many papers, with neutral descriptions as hard negatives. Evaluate per class and by unseen paper. Consider abstaining on uncertain sentiment until calibration on a separate development set demonstrates an acceptable false-opinion rate.',
 '5. **Reduce pairwise work before adding concurrency.** Restrict version candidates by sentence/list item and local distance, retain a no-link option, batch classifier examples, and avoid scoring all possible alias pairs. Measure candidate recall before pruning so speed gains do not silently remove correct links. Then evaluate shared encoder features or distillation. Parallelism across independent documents can help throughput, but it does not by itself remove the quadratic per-window work.',
 '6. **Build a trustworthy gold benchmark and training pool.** Repair source offsets, normalize the SoMeSci/SoFAIR/Softcite schemas, separate unknown from negative labels, and group splits by paper/DOI plus near-duplicate text. Use ecosyste.ms for sampling and candidate discovery, then annotate spans and attributes. Hold out an independently reviewed cross-domain test set before new training. More data may help; improvement and universal superiority must be demonstrated, not assumed.',
 '## Run integrity and limitations',
 'The main pass recorded nine HTTP 500 responses: four reference-paper windows in each Softcite arm, plus one SciBERT document-gold window. Both reference-paper services reported token/tokenization desynchronization on the same inputs. The document-gold failure arose in `SoftwareParser.refineTypes`. These are pipeline exceptions, not evidence of a learned domain restriction. Failures remain in the scheduled population; see [service failure evidence](service-failure-note.md).',
 'The reconstructed 012 training pool has no shared article IDs and no exact paragraphs after whitespace normalization with the 461 paragraph-gold inputs. This is not a near-duplicate audit. Training membership of the packaged Softcite checkpoints was not independently audited; the benchmark is the recovered published holdout subset available locally.',
 table(['Dataset','Model','Documents','Windows','Failed docs','Partial docs','Projection issues','Invalid reference offsets'],[[r['dataset'],LABEL[r['arm']],r['documents'],r['windows'],r['failed_documents'],r['partial_documents'],r['projection_issues'],r['invalid_reference_offsets']] for r in summaries if r['policy']==('native' if r['arm']=='ossomex012' else 'explicit')]),
 'Fulltext20, diverse full texts, dev190, and the five reference papers are included for extraction/operational diagnostics. They do not have exhaustive gold labels. The repaired SoMeSci/SoFAIR subsets reuse the same selected papers as the old broken imports and are not independent additional evidence. All remaining predicted spans outside positive-only references are unjudged, not automatically false positives. Main raw inference latencies include only inference and synchronization; JSON serialization and checkpoint loading are excluded.',
 'Softcite returns UTF-8 JSON with a text/plain response header. The inference recorder preserved its response bytes through Requests’ Latin1 decoding. Analysis reconstructs the original bytes and strictly decodes UTF-8; raw files remain unchanged. JSONL is split only on LF, avoiding accidental splitting on Unicode NEL inside response strings. See `encoding-recovery.json`. Excluded encoding and whitespace probes overlapped the first Wapiti quality pass; use the later isolated timing repeats for speed comparisons.',
 '## Reproducibility and evidence',
 '- `protocol.md`, `freeze.json`, `corrected/freeze.json`: frozen inputs, references, source hashes, and evaluation rules.\n- `engine-verification.json`: live container engines and weight hashes.\n- `scores.csv`, `corrected/scores.csv`: tabular scores.\n- `errors.csv`: exact-span false positives/negatives with source context.\n- `coverage-diagnostics.json`, `paired-bootstrap.json`, `timing-summary.json`: supplementary diagnostics.\n- Each dataset directory: inputs, windows, untouched raw responses, normalized predictions, projection issues, and field-level metrics.\n- `run.py`, `run_remaining.py`, `prepare_corrected.py`, `score.py`, `diagnostics.py`, `build_report.py`: run and analysis scripts.\n- Existing model source: `src/research/training/full_label.py` and `attribute_features.py`; adaptation source: `reports/scibert-v2/softcite-gold-001/scripts/train_detector.py`.']
 text='\n\n'.join(sections)+'\n';(OUT/'report.md').write_text(text)
 try:
  import markdown
  body=markdown.markdown(text,extensions=['tables','fenced_code'])
 except ImportError:body='<pre>'+html.escape(text)+'</pre>'
 (OUT/'report.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>OSSoMeX 012 comparison</title><style>body{font:16px/1.6 system-ui;max-width:1250px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 28px;color:#192430}h1,h2{line-height:1.25}h2{margin-top:42px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:13px}th,td{text-align:left;padding:7px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd}th{background:#eef2f5}code{font-size:90%}img{max-width:100%}</style></head><body>'+body+'</body></html>')
 print('report generated')
if __name__=='__main__':main()
